# Activity log + DescentReviewChanges dual-write

## 1. Daily activity log (DecenniumDescent-main only)

- Append to `docs/activity/YYYY-MM-DD.md` (create the file for today if missing).
- Log meaningful work briefly so progress survives crashes (what changed, why, open questions).
- **Never** copy activity logs into `DescentReviewChanges`.

## 2. Dual-write game changes to DescentReviewChanges

When editing **actual game / product** files:

1. Edit the real path in DecenniumDescent-main as usual.
2. Also copy the same file under `DescentReviewChanges/`, preserving relative path  
   (e.g. `docs/foo.md` → `DescentReviewChanges/docs/foo.md`).

### INCLUDE (copy to DescentReviewChanges)

- Player Rulebook, Director manuals, bestiary, cosmology, published game books
- Companion game data (JSON, spells, monsters, items, characters, floors, encounters, generators)
- Product UI/code that implements game features players/GMs use
- Anything the owner would periodically review as game content

### EXCLUDE (do not copy)

- Agent thinking logs, transcripts, scratchpads
- Daily activity logs / operational “what we did today” files
- Meta change-over notes, agent changelogs, process notes about the edit itself
- Cursor rules, agent instructions, continuity protocol docs (unless published as game books)
- Internal agent-ops tooling scripts (unless shipping product)
- Temporary notes / process-only TODOs

If ambiguous: **exclude** from DescentReviewChanges and note the choice in today’s activity log.
